{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `log_earn`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added top-level data variable `log_earn` so the originally scored transformed-data response is a SafeStan-protected top-level observation. In `data_safe.json`, `log_earn[i] = log(earn[i])` deterministically from the supplied `earn`. Removed the transformed-data computation of `log_earn`. Reordered the `sigma_a1`, `sigma_a2`, and `sigma_y` prior statements so `sigma_a1` and `sigma_a2` are given priors before being used in the priors for `a1` and `a2`. The original `earn`, `eth`, `height`, and `N` remain unprotected context data.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  vector[N] earn;
  vector[N] log_earn;
  array[N] int eth;
  vector[N] height;
}
parameters {
  vector[4] a1;
  vector[4] a2;
  real<lower=0> sigma_a1;
  real<lower=0> sigma_a2;
  real<lower=0> sigma_y;
  real mu_a1;
  real mu_a2;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[N] y_hat;

  for (i in 1 : N) {
    y_hat[i] = a1[eth[i]] + a2[eth[i]] * height[i];
  }
}
model {
  mu_a1 ~ normal(0, 1);
  mu_a2 ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_a1 ~ cauchy(0, 5);
  sigma_a2 ~ cauchy(0, 5);
  sigma_y ~ cauchy(0, 5);
  a1 ~ normal(10 * mu_a1, sigma_a1);
  a2 ~ normal(0.01 * mu_a2, sigma_a2);
  log_earn ~ normal(y_hat, sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N": 2, "earn": [6.059244407623112, 2.5406301932365647], "log_earn": [1.80158510709667, 0.932412157830352], "eth": [2, 2], "height": [4.895785758432679, 5.325827149546329]}","protected_variables":["log_earn"]}
